• Step 1 — Problem (1 sentence)
Study rooms get double-booked, cancellations waste rooms, and students don’t see
real-time availability.
• Step 1 – Answer
Study rooms are being double booked because students do not have room check in times.
And students are cancelling at the last minute, so rooms are being wasted. And a proper
system is not in place to see the availability of the rooms and the times the students are
checking in and out.
• Step 2 — System goal (2 sentences)
Write what the system does: booking + rules + reminders + reporting.
• Step 2 — System goal ASNWER (2 sentences)
The system allows students to book rooms, and it allows the Data Analyst to see how
frequently rooms are being used. And it allows students to the availability of the rooms.
• Step 3 — ANSWER IS roles (choose 3)
• Librarians
• Students
• IT Support
• Step 4 — ANSWER 4 components table
People/Tech/Process/Data.
People: Students, Librarians, IT Support, Data Analyst
Technology: Database, Booking website, Notifications
Process: Looking for availability, booking, access/denied, using the rooms
Data: student ID, days, hours of rooms being used, the time slots for students
Step 5 — ASNWER As-Is process (6 steps)
How do students currently reserve rooms?
1. Check for a room
2. Request for booking
3. Staff checks for availability to accept or decline
4. Students booking is recorded
5. No show for students
6. Rooms not being used
• Step 6 — ANSWER To-Be process with 2 decisions
Include decisions like:
o “Room available?”
o “User confirmed within 2 hours?”
1. Student selects room
2. Student selects a time
3. Student waits to get confirmed for a room
4. Student gets approved for a room
5. Student receives a notification
6. Booking Status gets updated (Staff can see & other students)
Decision 1: Room Available?
If no > choose another time/ or room > end.
If yes > select a time
Decision 2: “Did user confirm within 2 hours?”
If no > Booking is cancelled.
If yes > student booking is updated within the status
